<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96856" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῐχάομαι</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		, used by <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> only in 
			Ep.
		
		3pl.
		impf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐστιχόωντο</span>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στίξ, στείχω</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>march in rows</i> or <i>ranks</i>, esp. of
			soldiers, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.92
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.432
			</span></i>, etc.; of ships in line, <i><span class="en">
				2.516
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				602
			</span></i>, etc.; of herdsmen with their herds, <i><span class="en">
				18.577
			</span></i>; of cattle, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.126
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῆρας, ὅσαι στιχόωνται ἐπ᾽ ἀγρούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>L.</u>
					272
				</span></i>
			: of two persons <i>marching</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.266
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				341
			</span></i>.— 
				Act.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στιχάει</span> is prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.635
			</span></i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμοστιχάω</span>); later 
				Ep.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στιχόωσι</span>
			<i>stand in rows</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				191
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Mosch.
				2.142
			</span></i>; part. neut. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στιχόωντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					372
				</span></i>
			.</div>
